{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787234433,"nonce":"ogY2yPjguKBYHJCWGwxWNyRo2aY=","title":"**What is wrong.** The links overflow's `Show all labels` option is inert. `overflowMenu`","message":"(`internal/channels/render/slack/root.go`) mints it with a `value` of the form `labels|\u003cid\u003e`, which\nSPEC §H.8 designates for `views.open` — and no modal was ever built, so pressing it does nothing at\nall. Nothing errors and nothing is logged; the press is simply answered with silence.\n\n**The demonstration.** `grep -rn 'views.open' internal/channels` finds no call. `oto.more` reaches\n`Handle`'s inert arm (`internal/channels/service/interactions.go`), which is correct for the four\nlink options — they are `oto.noop.` destinations the Slack client opens itself — but `Show all labels`\nis not a link. It is the one option in that menu whose value asks oto to render something, and oto\nrenders nothing.\n\n**Why it matters.** SPEC §B.8.6 states the rule this breaks: *\"Buttons are never no-ops.\"* A menu\nentry that looks actionable and does nothing teaches an operator to distrust the card, which is the\nopposite of what a product whose premise is \"never lies\" can afford. It is also the reason `oto.more`\nwas previously mis-classified: commit `8b56e45` admitted `oto.more` to the closed action set so\nlink presses stop feeding `oto_slack_unknown_action_total`, and the runbook\n(`docs/runbooks/oto_slack_unknown_action_total.md`) now records that this half is\nknown-and-routed-but-unbuilt rather than unroutable. That note is a placeholder for this ticket.\n\n**Why a modal is not the answer.** `views.open` needs a `trigger_id` on §H.8's 3-second synchronous\npath — the exact constraint that made ticket `0a8ca4a` choose a `static_select` over a modal for the\nsnooze presets — and it is a second interaction type `parseSlackEnvelope` refuses by design.\n\n**Where.** `internal/channels/render/slack/root.go` (`overflowMenu`, the `labels|\u003cid\u003e` value) ·\n`internal/channels/service/interactions.go` (`ActionOverflow`'s inert arm) ·\n`docs/runbooks/oto_slack_unknown_action_total.md` (the known-gap note) · SPEC §B.8.6, §H.8.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** **Owner ruling, 2026-08-20: the press is answered with an ephemeral message listing\nthe labels**, not a modal — no `views.open`, no `trigger_id`, nothing on the synchronous path, which\nis consistent with how this package already answers an unavailable port with an honest ephemeral. The\nlabels are read-only, so an ephemeral is the whole feature. `oto.more`'s arm stops being inert for the\n`labels|` value while staying inert for the four `oto.noop.` links, the runbook's known-gap note is\nreplaced by what it now does, and a golden or handler test pins that a `labels|` press produces an\nephemeral naming every label.","files":null}]}